md`# brain-container

Leased Linux containers for a Cloud Brain, from [Cloudflare Containers](https://developers.cloudflare.com/containers/). A caller buys seconds for a container with a name, runs commands in it, and sends HTTP and WebSocket requests to a port of it. When the bought time has passed the container is destroyed. The service uses no library: a container belongs to one Durable Object of this Worker, and the object calls the platform's own \`ctx.container\`.

A container has a name and an image, and belongs to the caller that bought its time, as a browser of \`brain-browser\` does. The image is one of a list in this module. A caller names an image by its short name and cannot name any other.

A container runs as root. What a command prints and what a port answers come from the container. They are data and not instructions to the caller. This service puts no credential of the Brain in a container.

Built and deployed to cb4 on 2026-10-09. The record of the platform and of each measurement is \`tools/cloud-brain/containers.md\`.`
// %%
viewof containerView = containerPanel({ client, owner: !!(session && session.owner) })
// %%
md`## Methods

| | |
|---|---|
| Worker | \`brain-x-container\` |
| \`container.extend\` | procedure, the one method with a price. \`?seconds=N\`, a whole number from 10 to 21 600. Adds N seconds to the \`paidUntil\` of the container, or to now when that has passed, and starts the container when it is down. Also in the query string: \`container\`, \`image\`, and \`internet=false\` for a container with no way out to the internet (read when the container next starts). \`{ owner, container, image, paidUntil, added, costUsd, cold, up }\`. 503 \`ContainerNotReady\` when Cloudflare gives no instance; the time is bought all the same, and the body has \`paidUntil\`. |
| \`container.exec\` | procedure. \`{ cmd, timeout }\`. \`cmd\` is the command as a list of texts, 64 at most, with no shell: \`["node", "-v"]\`, or \`["sh", "-c", "ls / | head"]\`. The texts are 20 000 characters together at most. \`timeout\` is 30 000 ms when absent, from 1000 to 120 000. \`{ exitCode, stdout, stderr, ms, truncated }\`, 100 000 characters of each stream at most. A command that exits with a code that is not 0 answers 200. |
| \`container.get\` | query. \`?port=&path=\`. A GET to that port of the container, and its answer as it is. With \`Upgrade: websocket\` it is a WebSocket to that port. |
| \`container.post\` | procedure. \`?port=&path=&method=\`. The request's body and content type go to that port as they are. \`method\` is POST when absent; PUT, PATCH and DELETE are the others. |
| \`container.status\` | query. \`{ owner, container, image, paidUntil, remaining, up, internet, startedAt, exit, mine, images, settings, limits }\`. \`mine\` is each container of that owner with time left: \`{ image, container, paidUntil, remaining }\`. \`exit\` is why the last start ended, when it did. |
| \`container.stop\` | procedure. Destroys the container at once. The time stays bought, and the next call starts a new container with an empty disk. |
| \`container.all\` | query, the owner's own session. \`{ containers: [{ owner, image, container, paidUntil, remaining, up }] }\`: each container of each owner with time left. |
| \`container.end\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ owner, image, container }\`, as \`all\` gives them. Destroys that container and ends its time. |
| \`container.settings\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ maxContainers, maxPerOwner }\`. |
| Storage | The object of a container keeps \`lease\`: \`{ owner, name, image, internet, paidUntil }\`, and an alarm at \`paidUntil\`. \`rows\`: \`c/<owner>/<image>/<name>\` \`{ paidUntil }\` for the lists, and \`settings\`. |

Each method of the first six takes \`container\` and \`image\` in the query string: \`container\` is a name of 1 to 40 letters, digits, \`-\` and \`_\` that starts with a letter or a digit, \`default\` when absent. \`image\` is \`node\` when absent.

\`\`\`js
await client.procedure("container.extend", {}, { params: { seconds: 60 } })
// { owner: "owner", container: "default", image: "node", paidUntil: 1791570000000, added: 60, costUsd: 0.00012, cold: true, up: true }
await client.procedure("container.exec", { cmd: ["node", "-v"] })
// { exitCode: 0, stdout: "v22.…\\n", stderr: "", ms: 110, truncated: false }
// A server in the container, then a request to its port:
await client.procedure("container.exec", { cmd: ["sh", "-c", "nohup node -e 'require(\\"http\\").createServer((q,s)=>s.end(\\"hi\\")).listen(8080)' >/tmp/log 2>&1 &"] })
await client.fetch("container.get", { params: { port: 8080, path: "/" } })
\`\`\`

\`exec\`, \`get\` and \`post\` need bought time. With none they answer 409 \`NoTime\` with \`paidUntil\`. With time and the container down, they start it. A port that nothing listens on answers 502 \`NoListener\`; in the first 15 s after a start the call is tried again until the port answers.

\`seconds\`, \`container\` and \`image\` are in the query string and not in the body, because a price reads \`request.params\` and does not read the body, and because \`get\` and \`post\` pass the body on unread.`
// %%
md`## The pass-through

\`container.get\` and \`container.post\` are the container's own port. This Worker finds the object of the container from the caller's name and the two names in the query string, and hands it the request. The object holds \`paidUntil\` in its memory and gives the request to \`ctx.container.getTcpPort(port)\`. Neither reads the answer or a row. Neither reads the body, but for the first 15 s after a start, when the object keeps the body to send it again if the port does not answer yet. The object has two kinds of call, told apart by a host name this Worker writes: its own (\`extend\`, \`exec\`, \`stop\`, \`status\`) and a port. A \`path\` reaches the port whatever it is: \`/_extend\` is a path of the container's server and buys nothing. \`authorization\`, \`cookie\` and each \`x-brain-\` header are removed before the container sees the request. The core checks the rule and writes its one log line, as for each method.

A WebSocket is one call to \`container.get\` with \`Upgrade: websocket\`. The rule is decided one time, at the upgrade. The socket closes when the container is destroyed.

Use \`exec\` for one command with one answer. Use a port for a process that stays: a server in the container that the caller starts with \`exec\`.`
// %%
md`## Images

| name | image | type | $ a second | where |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| \`node\` | \`docker.io/library/node:22-alpine\` | lite: 1/16 vCPU, 256 MiB, 2 GB | 0.000002 ($0.0072 an hour) | \`WEUR\` |

Each image is one container application of the Cloudflare account, which the deployer makes when it deploys this Worker: \`<script>-<name>\`, scheduling policy \`default\`, 0 instances kept, \`max\` at most. An image is on Docker Hub. An application starts its image with the entrypoint in the list, which keeps the container up with nothing running in it.

To add an image, add it to \`containerImageList\`, remove the Worker and deploy it again: Cloudflare takes a new Durable Object class only with the upload of a script, and the deployer refuses the change on a Worker that runs. Removing the Worker deletes its applications and ends each container.

Not here: an image that runs a lopecode notebook. It has to be built and pushed with Docker, one time, to Docker Hub or to Cloudflare's registry.`
// %%
md`## Who can call, and what it costs

\`extend\`, \`exec\`, \`get\`, \`post\`, \`status\` and \`stop\` are \`who: "workers"\`: the owner, a token or an account the owner gave the method, and a Worker of this Brain that names the method in its \`calls\`. A member has none of them. \`all\`, \`end\` and \`settings\` are for the owner's own session, and the owner cannot put a different rule.

A container is the triple of its owner, its image and its name. The owner is the caller the core names. A call made for a person that is not their own tab (a turn, a PDS call, a portal) owns containers as \`via:<caller>\`, as in \`brain-browser\`.

The price of \`extend\` is \`seconds\` times the rate of the image, which is Cloudflare's price for the instance type at full use, rounded: lite is $0.000002015 a second from the three prices and the list charges $0.000002 ([pricing](https://developers.cloudflare.com/containers/pricing/), read 2026-10-09: memory $0.0000025 a GiB-second, CPU $0.000020 a vCPU-second, disk $0.00000007 a GB-second). Time that is bought is not given back: not when the container is stopped, and not when it never started.

| Setting | Default | |
|---|---|---|
| \`maxContainers\` | 6 | containers with time left, of all owners. Not more than the least \`max\` of the images, which is what Cloudflare runs. |
| \`maxPerOwner\` | 3 | containers with time left that one caller owns |

Over a limit, \`extend\` for a container that has no time left answers 429 \`TooManyContainers\`. The count is read and then the time is added, so two calls at one moment can pass the limit by one.`
// %%
md`## Limits

- **The disk is not kept.** A container that is destroyed, by the end of its time, by \`stop\` or by removing the Worker, starts again from its image.
- **A container that exits is started again by the next call**, with an empty disk, while time is left. \`status\` gives \`exit\`.
- **A new application gives no container at first.** 4 minutes in the spike, 27 s after the first deploy of this Worker (both 2026-10-09). \`extend\` in that time answers 503 and the time is bought all the same.
- **Egress.** A container reaches the internet unless its time was bought with \`internet=false\`. Nothing counts or limits what it sends; Cloudflare bills egress over 1 TB a month to the account.
- **\`exec\` gives the whole output when the command ends.** It does not stream. A command that is still running at \`timeout\` answers 504 \`ExecTimeout\`, and the command goes on in the container.
- **No file is put in a container by this service.** A caller writes one with \`exec\` or sends it to a port.
- **The container sees the caller's address.** \`cf-connecting-ip\`, \`cf-ipcountry\`, \`cf-ray\`, \`x-real-ip\` and the caller's own headers reach the port (seen 2026-10-09). \`authorization\`, \`cookie\` and \`x-brain-*\` do not.
- **Cloudflare keeps \`max\` instances of an image ready**, each already running the entrypoint: the application reported \`instances: 6\` and 6 healthy with no container leased, and the first container had been up 34 s when its time was bought. Its pricing page says charges start "when a request is sent to the container or when it is manually started". Whether the ready ones are billed was not seen on a bill.
- **A deploy of this Worker does not end a running container** (seen one time, 2026-10-09: a file in \`/tmp\` was still there and \`/proc/uptime\` went from 350 s to 415 s across an apply). The first try of that apply was put back after 60 s on a 504 from Cloudflare's version upload; the second deployed in 57 s. The cause of the 504 is not known.`
// %%
md`## Measured

On cb4, 2026-10-09, caller in Berlin. The record with each run is \`tools/cloud-brain/containers.md\`.

${containerMeasured}`
// %%
// Filled from tools/cloud-brain/containers.md after each measured run.
containerMeasured = `\`\`\`
first deploy 20:29:44 CEST: application made about 20:30:10, 5 instances ready at 20:30:37 (27 s; the spike waited 4 minutes)
extend, container down            0.62 s for the whole call; cold: true, up: true
exec ["node","-v"]                 v22.23.3, 223 ms inside the object (the first), 52 to 119 ms after
inside                             Linux 6.18.54-cloudflare-microvm, uid 0, 1 CPU, MemTotal 471032 kB, colo=DUB (regions: WEUR)

one connection, 25 calls each, p50 / p90 / least, ms
quota.get         (kernel, core)                  87 / 122 / 64
container.status  (+ service, object, 2 row reads) 120 / 153 / 102
container.get     (+ service, object, port 8080)  102 / 128 / 88
container.post    1 KB to the same port           101 / 156 / 90
container.exec    ["true"], 15 calls              127 / 176 / 118
the same server asked from inside the container   node's own start on 1/16 vCPU is 1.4 s; no figure for one request

WebSocket to port 8081 through container.get      open and first frame 435 ms after the client began
idle 113 s with no call                           the same container: /proc/uptime 201 s, its files in /tmp
time ended 20:33:50                               at 20:33:56 status up: false, exec and get 409 NoTime, container.all []
application health at 20:34:06                    active 0, healthy 6
a member / no caller                              403 no grant / 401
\`\`\`

\`container.get\` is 15 ms over a call the core answers itself. The spike, with the container in Istanbul and no region named, had 48 ms from the Worker to the port; with \`WEUR\` the container ran in Dublin.

A server a caller starts with \`exec\` needs its own time before it listens: the first \`get\`, 0.5 s after \`nohup node …\`, answered 502 \`NoListener\`. Seen one time each; nothing here was run twice but the series.`
// %%
container_service = cloudflare.Service("container", containerApp, {
  containers: { images: containerImageList, object: containerBox },
  methods: {
    // Time is bought by extend alone: get and post reach a port and no call of the object (see containerBox). The price is 0 for a number or an image the service refuses, so a refused call costs nothing.
    // who: "workers" is the owner, a token or an account the owner gave the method, and a Worker of this Brain. A member has none.
    "com.lopecode.brain.container.extend": { type: "procedure", who: "workers", price: containerPrice },
    ...Object.fromEntries(["exec", "post", "stop"].map((m) => ["com.lopecode.brain.container." + m, { type: "procedure", who: "workers" }])),
    ...Object.fromEntries(["get", "status"].map((m) => ["com.lopecode.brain.container." + m, { type: "query", who: "workers" }])),
    // all and end reach the containers of each owner. settings is the limits. The owner's own session only.
    "com.lopecode.brain.container.all": { type: "query", who: "owner", allow: "caller.session", fixed: true },
    "com.lopecode.brain.container.end": { type: "procedure", who: "owner", allow: "caller.session", fixed: true },
    "com.lopecode.brain.container.settings": { type: "procedure", who: "owner", allow: "caller.session", fixed: true }
  }
})
// %%
container_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", container_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced container_service";
}
// %%
// The images a caller can name. Each is one container application: image on Docker Hub, instance type, the most
// instances at one time, where it runs, and what a second costs at Cloudflare's price for that type at full use.
// The entrypoint keeps the container up; Cloudflare puts the image's own command after it, which sh takes as $0.
containerImageList = ({
  node: { image: "docker.io/library/node:22-alpine", type: "lite", max: 6, regions: ["WEUR"], entrypoint: ["sh", "-c", "exec tail -f /dev/null"], dollarsPerSecond: 0.000002 }
})
// %%
containerLimits = ({
  image: "node", // the image of a call that names none
  maxContainers: 6, // containers with time left, of all owners. Not more than the max of the image.
  maxPerOwner: 3,
  minSeconds: 10, // the least and the most one extend buys. The price reads the same two numbers.
  maxSeconds: 21600,
  startWait: 10000, // ms a call waits for a container that is starting
  listenGrace: 15000, // ms after a start in which a port that does not answer is tried again
  execTimeout: 30000, // ms
  maxTimeout: 120000, // ms
  execArgs: 64,
  execChars: 20000, // the command, all its texts together
  outputChars: 100000, // each of stdout and stderr
  keepRows: 86400 // seconds a row is kept after its time passed
})
// %%
containerSeconds = (text) => (typeof text === "string" && /^[0-9]{2,5}$/.test(text) && +text >= containerLimits.minSeconds && +text <= containerLimits.maxSeconds ? +text : null)
// %%
// seconds times the rate of the image the call names, or of the default image. 0 for what the service refuses.
containerPrice = {
  const L = containerLimits, rate = (name) => containerImageList[name].dollarsPerSecond;
  const byImage = Object.keys(containerImageList).sort().reduce((rest, name) => `(request.params.image == "${name}" ? ${rate(name)} : ${rest})`, "0.0");
  return `has(request.params.seconds) && request.params.seconds.matches("^[0-9]{2,5}$") && int(request.params.seconds) >= ${L.minSeconds} && int(request.params.seconds) <= ${L.maxSeconds} ? double(request.params.seconds) * (has(request.params.image) ? ${byImage} : ${rate(L.image)}) : 0.0`;
}
// %%
// What the Durable Object of one container does. ctx is the object's own: ctx.container is the container, ctx.storage
// keeps the lease, and the alarm is at paidUntil. The lease is read from storage once and then held in memory, so a
// request to a port reads nothing.
containerBox = {
  const L = containerLimits;
  const held = new WeakMap();
  const json = (value, status = 200) => new Response(JSON.stringify(value), { status, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
  const sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));
  const text = (bytes) => new TextDecoder().decode(bytes || new Uint8Array());
  const state = async (ctx) => {
    if (!held.has(ctx)) held.set(ctx, { lease: (await ctx.storage.get("lease")) || null, up: false, exit: null, startedAt: 0 });
    return held.get(ctx);
  };
  const paid = (s) => !!s.lease && Date.now() < s.lease.paidUntil;
  // Starts the container when it is down, and waits until it runs a command. False when Cloudflare gives none in time.
  const up = async (ctx, s) => {
    const c = ctx.container;
    let cold = false;
    if (!c.running) {
      cold = true;
      Object.assign(s, { up: false, exit: null, ending: false, startedAt: Date.now() });
      // Why the container ended, unless this object destroyed it.
      const over = (why) => void Object.assign(s, { up: false, exit: s.ending ? null : String(why).slice(0, 300) });
      try {
        c.start({ enableInternet: s.lease.internet !== false });
        c.monitor().then(() => over("exited"), (e) => over((e && e.message) || e));
      } catch (e) {
        over((e && e.message) || e);
      }
    }
    const until = Date.now() + L.startWait;
    while (!s.up && !s.exit && Date.now() < until) {
      try {
        await (await c.exec(["true"])).output();
        s.up = true;
      } catch (e) {
        s.last = String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 300);
        await sleep(100);
      }
    }
    return { cold, up: s.up };
  };
  const down = (s) => ({ error: "ContainerNotReady", message: `the container did not start: ${s.exit || s.last || "no answer"}. A new application has no instance for about 4 minutes. Call again.`, paidUntil: s.lease.paidUntil });
  const noTime = (s) => json({ error: "NoTime", message: "no time is bought for this container: container.extend?seconds=N", paidUntil: s.lease ? s.lease.paidUntil : 0 }, 409);
  const destroy = async (ctx, s) => {
    s.ending = true;
    if (ctx.container.running) await ctx.container.destroy();
    s.up = false;
  };
  const fetch = async (ctx, about, request) => {
    const url = new URL(request.url), s = await state(ctx), c = ctx.container;
    // Two hosts, and the service writes both: op.internal is this object's own calls, port-N.internal is port N of the
    // container. A caller gives a path and a port number, which are in neither host name.
    const op = url.hostname === "op.internal" ? url.pathname : null;
    const port = op ? 0 : +(url.hostname.match(/^port-([0-9]{1,5})\.internal$/) || [])[1];
    if (!op && !port) return json({ error: "InvalidRequest", message: "not a call of this object" }, 400);
    if (op === "/_status") return json({ paidUntil: s.lease ? s.lease.paidUntil : 0, remaining: s.lease ? Math.max(0, Math.round((s.lease.paidUntil - Date.now()) / 1000)) : 0, up: !!c.running, internet: s.lease ? s.lease.internet !== false : true, startedAt: c.running ? s.startedAt : 0, exit: s.exit });
    if (op === "/_extend") {
      const q = await request.json();
      const internet = q.internet === undefined ? (s.lease ? s.lease.internet !== false : true) : !!q.internet;
      s.lease = { owner: q.owner, name: q.name, image: about.image, internet, paidUntil: Math.max(Date.now(), s.lease ? s.lease.paidUntil : 0) + q.seconds * 1000 };
      await ctx.storage.put("lease", s.lease);
      await ctx.storage.setAlarm(s.lease.paidUntil);
      const started = await up(ctx, s);
      return started.up ? json({ paidUntil: s.lease.paidUntil, added: q.seconds, cold: started.cold, up: true }) : json(down(s), 503);
    }
    if (op === "/_stop" || op === "/_end") {
      await destroy(ctx, s);
      if (op === "/_end" && s.lease) {
        s.lease = { ...s.lease, paidUntil: Date.now() };
        await ctx.storage.put("lease", s.lease);
        await ctx.storage.deleteAlarm();
      }
      return json({ stopped: true, paidUntil: s.lease ? s.lease.paidUntil : 0 });
    }
    if (!paid(s)) return noTime(s);
    if (op && op !== "/_exec") return json({ error: "InvalidRequest", message: "not a call of this object" }, 400);
    if (op) {
      const q = await request.json(), t = Date.now();
      if (!(await up(ctx, s)).up) return json(down(s), 503);
      const done = await Promise.race([c.exec(q.cmd).then((p) => p.output()), sleep(q.timeout).then(() => null)]);
      if (!done) return json({ error: "ExecTimeout", message: `the command did not end in ${q.timeout} ms. It goes on in the container.` }, 504);
      const out = text(done.stdout), err = text(done.stderr);
      return json({ exitCode: done.exitCode, stdout: out.slice(0, L.outputChars), stderr: err.slice(0, L.outputChars), ms: Date.now() - t, truncated: out.length > L.outputChars || err.length > L.outputChars });
    }
    // A request to a port of the container, with the path as the caller gave it.
    if (!s.up || !c.running) if (!(await up(ctx, s)).up) return json(down(s), 503);
    const send = (r) => c.getTcpPort(port).fetch(new Request("http://box" + url.pathname + url.search, r));
    // Just after a start the process may not listen yet: the request is kept and tried again. After that it is passed once, unread.
    const fresh = Date.now() - s.startedAt < L.listenGrace;
    const kept = fresh && request.body ? await request.arrayBuffer() : null;
    const again = () => (kept ? new Request(request, { body: kept }) : request);
    for (;;) {
      try {
        return await send(fresh ? again() : request);
      } catch (e) {
        if (!fresh || Date.now() - s.startedAt >= L.listenGrace) return json({ error: "NoListener", message: `nothing answered on port ${port} of the container: ${String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 200)}` }, 502);
        await sleep(200);
      }
    }
  };
  // The alarm is at paidUntil. extend moves paidUntil, so an alarm that comes early sets itself again.
  const alarm = async (ctx) => {
    const s = await state(ctx);
    if (s.lease && Date.now() < s.lease.paidUntil) return void (await ctx.storage.setAlarm(s.lease.paidUntil));
    await destroy(ctx, s);
  };
  return { fetch, alarm };
}
// %%
// A container is the triple of who owns it, its image and its name. Its object is "<owner>/<name>" of the image's class.
// rows: c/<owner>/<image>/<name> { paidUntil } is written by extend and read by the lists, never by exec, get or post.
containerOps = {
  const L = containerLimits;
  const stop = (status, error, message, more) => Object.assign(new Error(message), { status, error, more });
  const named = (name, what) => {
    if (typeof name !== "string" || !/^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,39}$/.test(name)) throw stop(400, "InvalidRequest", what + ": 1 to 40 letters, digits, - and _");
    return name;
  };
  const imaged = (image = L.image) => {
    if (typeof image !== "string" || !Object.hasOwn(containerImageList, image)) throw stop(400, "InvalidRequest", "image: one of " + Object.keys(containerImageList).sort().join(", "));
    return image;
  };
  // Cloudflare gives an image no more instances than its max, so no more containers than the least max have time.
  const most = Math.min(...Object.values(containerImageList).map((i) => i.max));
  const settings = async () => {
    const set = (await rows.get("settings")) || {};
    return { maxContainers: Math.min(set.maxContainers || L.maxContainers, most), maxPerOwner: set.maxPerOwner || L.maxPerOwner };
  };
  // Each row with time left, as { owner, image, container, paidUntil, remaining }. A row a day past its time is deleted.
  const live = async () => {
    const now = Date.now(), out = [];
    for (const r of await rows.list("c/")) {
      const m = r.key.match(/^c\/([^/]+)\/([^/]+)\/([^/]+)$/);
      if (!m) continue;
      if (r.value.paidUntil > now) out.push({ owner: m[1], image: m[2], container: m[3], paidUntil: r.value.paidUntil, remaining: Math.round((r.value.paidUntil - now) / 1000) });
      else if (r.value.paidUntil < now - L.keepRows * 1000) await rows.delete(r.key);
    }
    return out;
  };
  const one = (who, name = "default", image) => {
    // A call with no caller has no owner: a rule that lets everyone in must not put them all in one container.
    if (who === "anonymous") throw stop(401, "AuthRequired", "a container has an owner. This call has no caller.");
    const owner = String(who).replace(/\//g, "_"), label = named(name, "container"), kind = imaged(image), key = `c/${owner}/${kind}/${label}`;
    // op is a call of the object itself. port is a request to a port of the container. They differ in the host name.
    const to = (host, path, init) => containers.fetch(kind, owner + "/" + label, new Request("http://" + host + path, init));
    const op = (path, init) => to("op.internal", path, init), port = (n, path, init) => to(`port-${n}.internal`, path, init);
    const ask = async (path, body) => {
      const r = await op(path, body === undefined ? {} : { method: "POST", body: JSON.stringify(body), headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
      const data = await r.json();
      if (!r.ok) throw stop(r.status, data.error, data.message, { paidUntil: data.paidUntil });
      return data;
    };
    return {
      op,
      port,
      extend: async ({ seconds, internet }) => {
        const n = containerSeconds(seconds);
        if (n == null) throw stop(400, "InvalidRequest", `seconds: a whole number from ${L.minSeconds} to ${L.maxSeconds}, in the query string`);
        const up = await live(), limits = await settings();
        if (!up.some((c) => c.owner === owner && c.image === kind && c.container === label)) {
          if (up.length >= limits.maxContainers) throw stop(429, "TooManyContainers", `${up.length} containers have time left and maxContainers is ${limits.maxContainers}`);
          if (up.filter((c) => c.owner === owner).length >= limits.maxPerOwner) throw stop(429, "TooManyContainers", `${owner} has ${limits.maxPerOwner} containers with time left, which is maxPerOwner`);
        }
        const r = await op("/_extend", { method: "POST", body: JSON.stringify({ owner, name: label, seconds: n, ...(internet === undefined ? {} : { internet }) }), headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
        const data = await r.json();
        // The time is bought when the container did not start, too.
        if (data.paidUntil) await rows.put(key, { paidUntil: data.paidUntil });
        if (!r.ok) throw stop(r.status, data.error, data.message, { paidUntil: data.paidUntil });
        return { owner, container: label, image: kind, paidUntil: data.paidUntil, added: n, costUsd: +(n * containerImageList[kind].dollarsPerSecond).toFixed(8), cold: data.cold, up: data.up };
      },
      exec: async ({ cmd, timeout = L.execTimeout }) => {
        if (!Array.isArray(cmd) || !cmd.length || cmd.length > L.execArgs || cmd.some((a) => typeof a !== "string") || cmd.join("").length > L.execChars) throw stop(400, "InvalidRequest", `cmd: a list of 1 to ${L.execArgs} texts, ${L.execChars} characters together`);
        if (!Number.isInteger(timeout) || timeout < 1000 || timeout > L.maxTimeout) throw stop(400, "InvalidRequest", `timeout: 1000 to ${L.maxTimeout} ms`);
        return ask("/_exec", { cmd, timeout });
      },
      status: async () => ({ owner, container: label, image: kind, ...(await ask("/_status")), mine: (await live()).filter((c) => c.owner === owner).map(({ owner: _, ...c }) => c), images: Object.entries(containerImageList).map(([name, i]) => ({ name, image: i.image, type: i.type, dollarsPerSecond: i.dollarsPerSecond })), settings: await settings(), limits: L }),
      stop: () => ask("/_stop", {}),
      end: async () => {
        const out = await ask("/_end", {});
        await rows.delete(key);
        return { ended: true, owner, image: kind, container: label, paidUntil: out.paidUntil };
      }
    };
  };
  return {
    one,
    most,
    all: async () => ({ containers: await Promise.all((await live()).map(async (c) => ({ ...c, up: await one(c.owner, c.container, c.image).op("/_status").then((r) => r.json()).then((s) => !!s.up, () => null) }))) }),
    settings: async (q) => {
      const next = await settings();
      for (const k of Object.keys(next)) {
        if (q[k] === undefined) continue;
        const top = k === "maxContainers" ? most : 20;
        if (!Number.isInteger(q[k]) || q[k] < 1 || q[k] > top) throw stop(400, "InvalidRequest", `${k}: a whole number from 1 to ${top}`);
        next[k] = q[k];
      }
      await rows.put("settings", next);
      return next;
    }
  };
}
// %%
containerApp = {
  const app = new hono.Hono();
  const NS = "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.container.";
  // The core names the caller. This service records it and decides nothing.
  const by = (c) => c.req.header("x-brain-caller") || "anonymous";
  const body = async (c) => {
    const b = await c.req.json().catch(() => null);
    return b && typeof b === "object" ? b : {};
  };
  const fail = (c, e) => c.json({ error: e.error, message: e.message, ...e.more }, e.status);
  const answer = (fn) => async (c) => {
    try {
      const out = await fn(c);
      return out instanceof Response ? out : c.json(out);
    } catch (e) {
      if (e && e.status) return fail(c, e);
      throw e;
    }
  };
  // Who owns the container: the caller, or via:<caller> for a call that is not that person's own tab (see brain-browser).
  const who = (c) => (by(c) !== "anonymous" && /^(turn:|portal:|jwt$)/.test(c.req.header("x-brain-via") || "") ? "via:" + by(c) : by(c));
  // The price and a rule read the query string as the core does: of a name given two times, the last. The core
  // refuses such a call; this service reads the same one all the same.
  const last = (c, name) => new URL(c.req.url).searchParams.getAll(name).pop();
  const mine = (c) => containerOps.one(who(c), last(c, "container") || "default", last(c, "image"));
  app.post(NS + "extend", answer((c) => mine(c).extend({ seconds: last(c, "seconds"), ...(last(c, "internet") === undefined ? {} : { internet: last(c, "internet") !== "false" }) })));
  app.post(NS + "exec", answer(async (c) => mine(c).exec(await body(c))));
  app.post(NS + "stop", answer((c) => mine(c).stop()));
  app.get(NS + "status", answer((c) => mine(c).status()));
  // The pass-through. The request goes to the object of the container with its body unread; the object gives it to the port.
  const METHODS = ["POST", "PUT", "PATCH", "DELETE"];
  const pass = (c, method) => {
    const port = +last(c, "port"), path = last(c, "path") || "/";
    if (!Number.isInteger(port) || port < 1 || port > 65535) return c.json({ error: "InvalidRequest", message: "port: 1 to 65535, in the query string" }, 400);
    if (!path.startsWith("/") || !METHODS.concat("GET").includes(method)) return c.json({ error: "InvalidRequest", message: "path starts with /; method is one of " + METHODS.join(", ") }, 400);
    const headers = new Headers(c.req.raw.headers);
    for (const name of [...headers.keys()]) if (name === "authorization" || name === "cookie" || name.startsWith("x-brain-")) headers.delete(name);
    return mine(c).port(port, path, { method, headers, body: method === "GET" ? undefined : c.req.raw.body, ...(method === "GET" ? {} : { duplex: "half" }) });
  };
  app.get(NS + "get", answer((c) => pass(c, "GET")));
  app.post(NS + "post", answer((c) => pass(c, (last(c, "method") || "POST").toUpperCase())));
  // For the owner's own session, by the rule of each.
  app.get(NS + "all", answer(() => containerOps.all()));
  app.post(NS + "end", answer(async (c) => {
    const q = await body(c);
    if (typeof q.owner !== "string" || !q.owner) return c.json({ error: "InvalidRequest", message: "owner, image and container, as container.all gives them" }, 400);
    return containerOps.one(q.owner, q.container, q.image).end();
  }));
  app.post(NS + "settings", answer(async (c) => containerOps.settings(await body(c))));
  return app;
}
// %%
containerPanel = ({ client, owner = false } = {}) => {
  if (!client || !owner) return Object.assign(htl.html`<i style="color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)">Sign in to a Brain as the owner to see its containers.</i>`, { value: null });
  const el = htl.html`<div></div>`, state = htl.html`<div style="margin:6px 0"></div>`, fleet = htl.html`<div style="margin:6px 0"></div>`;
  const note = htl.html`<pre style="color:var(--theme-foreground-muted);margin-top:6px;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></pre>`;
  const say = (text) => void (note.textContent = text);
  const which = Inputs.text({ label: "Container", value: "default", width: "12em" });
  const image = Inputs.select(Object.keys(containerImageList), { label: "Image", value: containerLimits.image });
  const seconds = Inputs.number({ label: "Seconds to add", value: 60, min: containerLimits.minSeconds, max: containerLimits.maxSeconds, step: 1, width: "8em" });
  const cost = htl.html`<span style="align-self:center;color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)"></span>`;
  const command = Inputs.text({ label: "Command (sh -c)", placeholder: "node -v", width: "30em" });
  const limits = { maxContainers: Inputs.number({ label: "Containers with time", min: 1, max: Math.min(...Object.values(containerImageList).map((i) => i.max)), step: 1, width: "8em" }), maxPerOwner: Inputs.number({ label: "Containers of one caller", min: 1, max: 20, step: 1, width: "8em" }) };
  const P = () => ({ container: which.value || "default", image: image.value });
  // The price is on the page before the button is pressed. Time that is bought is not given back.
  const priced = () => void (cost.textContent = `${seconds.value} s costs $${Number(((Number(seconds.value) || 0) * containerImageList[image.value].dollarsPerSecond).toFixed(6))}, charged to your day. It is not given back.`);
  let fleetTable = null;
  const draw = async () => {
    const s = await client.query("container.status", P());
    el.value = s;
    el.dispatchEvent(new Event("input"));
    state.replaceChildren(htl.html`${s.remaining ? `${s.remaining} s are bought for ${s.container} (${s.image}).` : `No time is bought for ${s.container} (${s.image}).`} The container is ${s.up ? "up" : "down"}.${s.exit ? " Its last start ended: " + s.exit : ""}`);
    const every = (await client.query("container.all")).containers;
    fleetTable = Inputs.table(every.map((c) => ({ owner: c.owner, image: c.image, container: c.container, up: c.up, remaining: c.remaining })), { multiple: false, required: false, layout: "auto" });
    fleet.replaceChildren(every.length ? fleetTable : htl.html`<i style="color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)">No container has time.</i>`);
    for (const k in limits) limits[k].value = s.settings[k];
  };
  const run = (what, fn) => async () => {
    try {
      say(what + "…");
      say((await fn()) || "");
      await draw();
    } catch (e) {
      say(`${what} failed: ${(e && e.message) || e}`);
    }
  };
  const redraw = () => draw().catch((e) => say("container.status failed: " + ((e && e.message) || e)));
  for (const input of [which, image]) input.addEventListener("input", () => (priced(), redraw()));
  seconds.addEventListener("input", priced);
  priced();
  redraw();
  const refresh = Inputs.button("Refresh", { reduce: run("Refresh", async () => "") });
  const extend = Inputs.button("Add time", { reduce: run("Add time", async () => ((r) => `${r.added} s added, $${r.costUsd}${r.cold ? ", started" : ""}`)(await client.procedure("container.extend", {}, { params: { seconds: String(seconds.value), ...P() } }))) });
  const exec = Inputs.button("Run", { reduce: run("Run", async () => ((r) => `exit ${r.exitCode}, ${r.ms} ms\n${r.stdout}${r.stderr}`.slice(0, 4000))(await client.procedure("container.exec", { cmd: ["sh", "-c", command.value] }, { params: P() }))) });
  const stop = Inputs.button("Stop", { reduce: run("Stop", async () => void (await client.procedure("container.stop", {}, { params: P() }))) });
  const endOne = Inputs.button("End chosen container", {
    reduce: run("End", async () => {
      const row = fleetTable && fleetTable.value;
      if (!row) throw new Error("choose a container in the table");
      await client.procedure("container.end", { owner: row.owner, image: row.image, container: row.container });
    })
  });
  const save = Inputs.button("Save limits", { reduce: run("Save", async () => void (await client.procedure("container.settings", Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(limits).map(([k, i]) => [k, i.value]))))) });
  const rowOf = (...items) => htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:8px 0">${items}</div>`;
  el.append(which, image, state, rowOf(refresh, stop), seconds, rowOf(extend, cost), command, rowOf(exec), fleet, rowOf(endOne), ...Object.values(limits), rowOf(save), note);
  return el;
}
// %%
md`## Tests

The service runs here as the emitted Worker with its emitted object class, over a fake of \`ctx.container\`. The fake starts, runs a command by echoing it, and answers on the ports a test gives it. It does not run Linux.`
// %%
// ctx.container of each object, as "image/id" -> c. A test sets c.refuse to a message for a start Cloudflare refuses,
// and c.ports[N] to a function of a Request for a process that listens.
containerFake = () => {
  const made = new Map(), bytes = (t) => new TextEncoder().encode(t);
  const factory = (image, id) => {
    const key = image + "/" + id;
    if (made.has(key)) return made.get(key);
    const c = {
      running: false, starts: [], execs: [], destroyed: 0, refuse: null, ports: {}, over: null,
      start(options = {}) {
        if (c.refuse) return void (c.over = Promise.reject(new Error(c.refuse)));
        c.running = true;
        c.starts.push(options);
        c.over = new Promise(() => {});
      },
      monitor: () => c.over,
      destroy: async () => void ((c.running = false), c.destroyed++),
      exec: async (cmd) => {
        if (!c.running) throw new Error("the container is not running");
        c.execs.push(cmd);
        if (cmd[0] === "hang") return { output: () => new Promise(() => {}) };
        return { output: async () => ({ stdout: bytes(cmd[0] === "big" ? "x".repeat(150000) : cmd.join(" ") + "\n"), stderr: bytes(""), exitCode: cmd[0] === "false" ? 1 : 0 }) };
      },
      getTcpPort: (port) => ({
        fetch: async (request) => {
          if (!c.running || !c.ports[port]) throw new Error("connection refused");
          return c.ports[port](request);
        }
      })
    };
    made.set(key, c);
    return c;
  };
  return { factory, made, of: (id = "owner/default", image = "node") => factory(image, id) };
}
// %%
containerRig = async () => {
  const fake = containerFake();
  const sim = await simulate(container_service, { containers: fake.factory });
  const X = "https://brain.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.container.";
  const as = (who, via) => {
    const headers = { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": who, "x-brain-context": "for " + who, "x-brain-origin": who, ...(via ? { "x-brain-via": via } : {}) };
    const read = async (r) => ({ status: r.status, data: (r.headers.get("content-type") || "").includes("json") ? await r.json() : await r.text(), headers: r.headers });
    const query = (params) => (Object.keys(params).length ? "?" + new URLSearchParams(params) : "");
    return {
      get: async (m, params = {}, more = {}) => read(await sim.fetch(X + m + query(params), { headers: { ...headers, ...more } })),
      post: async (m, body = {}, params = {}, more = {}) => read(await sim.fetch(X + m + query(params), { method: "POST", body: typeof body === "string" ? body : JSON.stringify(body), headers: { ...headers, ...more } }))
    };
  };
  const box = (id = "owner/default", image = "node") => sim.boxes.get(image + "/" + id);
  return {
    sim, fake, as, owner: as("owner"), box,
    // The lease of an object as its storage has it, and a way to move its end: the object forgets what it held in memory,
    // as one that Cloudflare put to sleep does, and reads the lease again.
    lease: (id, image) => box(id, image).stored.get("lease"),
    endsIn: (seconds, id, image) => {
      const b = box(id, image);
      b.stored.set("lease", { ...b.stored.get("lease"), paidUntil: Date.now() + seconds * 1000 });
      b.sleep();
    },
    price: async (params = {}) => {
      const rule = (await container_service.emit()).meta.access["com.lopecode.brain.container.extend"];
      const context = { caller: callerOf({ caller: "owner" }), request: { params } };
      // The price in millionths of a dollar, found by halving.
      let low = 0, high = 1 << 20;
      while (low < high) {
        const mid = (low + high) >> 1;
        if (decide({ allow: `(${rule.price}) < ${(mid + 0.5) / 1e6}` }, context).allow) high = mid;
        else low = mid + 1;
      }
      return low / 1e6;
    }
  };
}
// %%
test_container_declares_its_images_and_who_calls = {
  const { meta, parts } = await container_service.emit();
  expect(meta).toMatchObject({ worker: "brain-x-container", role: "recipe", module: "@tomlarkworthy/brain-container", resources: ["containers", "rows"], secrets: [], paths: [], calls: [], crons: [] });
  // One application and one object class for each image, and the class is bound to the Worker.
  expect(meta.containers).toEqual([{ name: "node", class_name: "Box_node", image: "docker.io/library/node:22-alpine", instance_type: "lite", max_instances: 6, entrypoint: ["sh", "-c", "exec tail -f /dev/null"], regions: ["WEUR"] }]);
  expect(meta.bindings).toContainEqual({ type: "durable_object_namespace", name: "BOX_NODE", class_name: "Box_node" });
  expect(parts[0].text).toContain("export class Box_node extends __DO");
  const callers = { owner: { caller: "owner", via: "session" }, token: { caller: "token:laptop" }, granted: { caller: "did:plc:ada" }, worker: { caller: "worker:brain-x-reader" }, anyone: { caller: "anonymous" } };
  const through = (rule) => Object.entries(callers).filter(([, w]) => decide(rule, { caller: callerOf(w), request: { method: "", path: "", verb: "POST", params: {} } }).allow).map(([n]) => n).join(" ");
  const N = "com.lopecode.brain.container.";
  for (const m of ["extend", "exec", "get", "post", "status", "stop"]) expect([m, through(meta.access[N + m])]).toEqual([m, "owner token granted worker"]);
  for (const m of ["all", "end", "settings"]) expect([m, through(meta.access[N + m]), meta.access[N + m].fixed]).toEqual([m, "owner", true]);
  expect(Object.keys(meta.access).filter((k) => meta.access[k].price).map((k) => k.slice(N.length))).toEqual(["extend"]);
  return Object.keys(meta.access).length + " methods, " + meta.containers.length + " image";
}
// %%
test_container_time_is_bought_by_extend_and_starts_it = {
  const rig = await containerRig();
  // No time: nothing runs, and nothing starts.
  expect((await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["node", "-v"] })).data).toMatchObject({ error: "NoTime", paidUntil: 0 });
  expect((await rig.owner.get("get", { port: 8080 })).status).toBe(409);
  expect(rig.fake.of().starts).toEqual([]);
  const t = Date.now();
  const first = await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60 });
  expect(first.data).toMatchObject({ owner: "owner", container: "default", image: "node", added: 60, costUsd: 0.00012, cold: true, up: true });
  expect(first.data.paidUntil - t).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(60000);
  expect(rig.fake.of().starts).toEqual([{ enableInternet: true }]);
  // The object keeps the lease and an alarm at its end; the row is for the lists.
  expect(rig.lease()).toEqual({ owner: "owner", name: "default", image: "node", internet: true, paidUntil: first.data.paidUntil });
  expect(rig.box().alarm).toBe(first.data.paidUntil);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.get("c/owner/node/default")).toEqual({ paidUntil: first.data.paidUntil });
  // More time is added to the end, and a container that is up is not started again.
  const more = await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 30 });
  expect([more.data.paidUntil - first.data.paidUntil, more.data.cold, rig.fake.of().starts.length, rig.box().alarm]).toEqual([30000, false, 1, more.data.paidUntil]);
  // seconds is read from the query string alone, and a number outside the limits buys nothing.
  for (const seconds of ["9", "21601", "1.5", "abc", ""]) expect([seconds, (await rig.owner.post("extend", { seconds: 60 }, seconds ? { seconds } : {})).status]).toEqual([seconds, 400]);
  expect(rig.lease().paidUntil).toBe(more.data.paidUntil);
  // A name given two times: the service reads the last, as the price does. No time at the price of an image that is not one.
  const twice = await rig.sim.fetch("https://brain.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.container.extend?seconds=60&image=node&image=other&container=a&container=b", { method: "POST", body: "{}", headers: { "x-brain-caller": "owner" } });
  expect([twice.status, (await twice.json()).message, [...rig.sim.boxes.keys()]]).toEqual([400, "image: one of node", ["node/owner/default"]]);
  // The price is seconds times the rate of the image, and 0 for what is refused.
  expect([await rig.price({ seconds: "60" }), await rig.price({ seconds: "3600", image: "node" }), await rig.price({ seconds: "9" }), await rig.price({ seconds: "60", image: "other" }), await rig.price({})]).toEqual([0.00012, 0.0072, 0, 0, 0]);
  return "90 s bought, 1 start";
}
// %%
test_container_exec_runs_a_command_in_the_callers_container = {
  const rig = await containerRig();
  await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60 });
  const out = await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["node", "-v"] });
  expect(out.data).toMatchObject({ exitCode: 0, stdout: "node -v\n", stderr: "", truncated: false });
  // A command that fails is an answer, not an error.
  expect((await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["false"] })).data).toMatchObject({ exitCode: 1 });
  expect((await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["big"] })).data).toMatchObject({ truncated: true });
  expect((await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["big"] })).data.stdout.length).toBe(containerLimits.outputChars);
  // The command is a list of texts: no shell reads it here.
  for (const cmd of ["node -v", [], [1], Array(65).fill("a"), ["x".repeat(20001)]]) expect((await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd })).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["true"], timeout: 500 })).status).toBe(400);
  // A command that does not end answers at the timeout.
  const slow = await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["hang"], timeout: 1000 });
  expect([slow.status, slow.data.error]).toEqual([504, "ExecTimeout"]);
  // A container that exited is started again by the next call while time is left.
  rig.fake.of().running = false;
  expect((await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["true"] })).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.fake.of().starts.length).toBe(2);
  return "exec, 2 starts";
}
// %%
test_container_get_and_post_are_the_port_and_read_no_row = {
  const rig = await containerRig();
  await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60 });
  const seen = [];
  rig.fake.of().ports[8080] = async (request) => {
    seen.push({ method: request.method, url: request.url, headers: Object.fromEntries(request.headers), body: request.method === "GET" ? null : await request.text() });
    return new Response("hello from the box", { status: 201, headers: { "content-type": "text/plain", "x-from": "box" } });
  };
  // Each row call of the Worker from here on is counted.
  let rowCalls = 0;
  const sql = rig.sim.env.SQL.sim;
  rig.sim.env.SQL = { sim: (...a) => (rowCalls++, sql(...a)) };
  const got = await rig.owner.get("get", { port: 8080, path: "/a/b?q=1" }, { authorization: "Bearer secret", cookie: "c=1", "x-brain-session": "s", "x-mine": "kept" });
  // The answer is the container's own: status, headers and body.
  expect([got.status, got.data, got.headers.get("x-from")]).toEqual([201, "hello from the box", "box"]);
  expect([seen[0].method, seen[0].url, seen[0].headers["x-mine"]]).toEqual(["GET", "http://box/a/b?q=1", "kept"]);
  // No credential of the Brain and no header of the core reaches the container.
  expect(Object.keys(seen[0].headers).filter((h) => h === "authorization" || h === "cookie" || h.startsWith("x-brain-"))).toEqual([]);
  const sent = await rig.owner.post("post", "raw bytes, not JSON", { port: 8080, path: "/in" }, { "content-type": "text/plain" });
  expect([sent.status, seen[1].method, seen[1].url, seen[1].body, seen[1].headers["content-type"]]).toEqual([201, "POST", "http://box/in", "raw bytes, not JSON", "text/plain"]);
  expect((await rig.owner.post("post", "{}", { port: 8080, method: "put" })).status).toBe(201);
  expect(seen[2].method).toBe("PUT");
  // Three requests to the port read and wrote no row.
  expect(rowCalls).toBe(0);
  // A path that is the name of one of the object's own calls is a path of the port. The lease and the container stay.
  const before = JSON.stringify(rig.lease()), reached = seen.length;
  for (const path of ["/_extend", "/_end", "/_stop", "/_status", "/_exec"]) {
    const g = await rig.owner.get("get", { port: 8080, path });
    const p = await rig.owner.post("post", JSON.stringify({ owner: "x", name: "y", seconds: 1000000, cmd: ["id"] }), { port: 8080, path });
    expect([path, g.status, g.data, p.status, p.data]).toEqual([path, 201, "hello from the box", 201, "hello from the box"]);
  }
  expect(seen.slice(reached).map((r) => r.url)).toEqual(["/_extend", "/_end", "/_stop", "/_status", "/_exec"].flatMap((p) => ["http://box" + p, "http://box" + p]));
  expect([JSON.stringify(rig.lease()), rig.fake.of().running, rig.fake.of().destroyed, rig.fake.of().execs.some((e) => e[0] === "id"), [...rig.sim.boxes.keys()]]).toEqual([before, true, 0, false, ["node/owner/default"]]);
  expect(rowCalls).toBe(0);
  // A host name that is neither is no call of the object.
  expect((await rig.box().object.fetch(new Request("http://box.internal/_extend", { method: "POST", body: "{}" }))).status).toBe(400);
  // A port, a path or a method the service refuses.
  for (const params of [{}, { port: 0 }, { port: 70000 }, { port: "http" }, { port: 8080, path: "no-slash" }]) expect((await rig.owner.get("get", params)).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await rig.owner.post("post", "", { port: 8080, method: "TRACE" })).status).toBe(400);
  // Nothing listens: 502 once the start is not fresh.
  rig.box().sleep();
  const none = await rig.owner.get("get", { port: 9 });
  expect([none.status, none.data.error]).toEqual([502, "NoListener"]);
  return seen.length + " requests reached the port";
}
// %%
test_container_is_destroyed_when_its_time_ends = {
  const rig = await containerRig();
  await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60 });
  const c = rig.fake.of();
  // An alarm that comes while time is left destroys nothing and sets itself again.
  rig.box().alarm = null;
  await rig.box().object.alarm();
  expect([c.running, c.destroyed, rig.box().alarm]).toEqual([true, 0, rig.lease().paidUntil]);
  // The time ends. The object was asleep: it reads the lease from its storage.
  rig.endsIn(-1);
  await rig.box().object.alarm();
  expect([c.running, c.destroyed]).toEqual([false, 1]);
  // Nothing starts it again without time.
  expect((await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["true"] })).data).toMatchObject({ error: "NoTime" });
  expect((await rig.owner.get("get", { port: 8080 })).status).toBe(409);
  expect(c.starts.length).toBe(1);
  expect((await rig.owner.get("status")).data).toMatchObject({ remaining: 0, up: false });
  // stop destroys at once and the time stays; end takes the time too.
  await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60 });
  expect((await rig.owner.post("stop")).data).toMatchObject({ stopped: true });
  expect([c.running, (await rig.owner.get("status")).data.remaining > 50]).toEqual([false, true]);
  await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["true"] });
  expect(c.running).toBe(true);
  expect((await rig.owner.post("end", { owner: "owner", image: "node", container: "default" })).data).toMatchObject({ ended: true });
  expect([c.running, rig.box().alarm, rig.sim.rows.has("c/owner/node/default"), (await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["true"] })).status]).toEqual([false, null, false, 409]);
  return "destroyed " + c.destroyed + " times";
}
// %%
test_container_each_caller_has_its_own_and_a_caller_names_no_image = {
  const rig = await containerRig();
  const reader = rig.as("worker:brain-x-reader"), turn = rig.as("owner", "turn:7");
  await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60 });
  await reader.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60 });
  await turn.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60, container: "job" });
  expect([...rig.sim.boxes.keys()].sort()).toEqual(["node/owner/default", "node/via:owner/job", "node/worker:brain-x-reader/default"]);
  // A caller reaches its own container by the same name, and no parameter names another owner's.
  await reader.post("exec", { cmd: ["id"] });
  expect([rig.fake.of("worker:brain-x-reader/default").execs.filter((e) => e[0] === "id").length, rig.fake.of().execs.filter((e) => e[0] === "id").length]).toEqual([1, 0]);
  expect((await reader.get("status", { owner: "owner" })).data).toMatchObject({ owner: "worker:brain-x-reader", mine: [{ image: "node", container: "default" }] });
  // A call with no caller has no container.
  expect((await rig.as("anonymous").post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60 })).status).toBe(401);
  // An image is a name of the list. Anything else is refused, and so is a name that is not a name.
  for (const image of ["docker.io/library/alpine:3", "Node", "other"]) expect([image, (await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60, image })).data.message]).toEqual([image, "image: one of node"]);
  for (const container of ["a/b", "-a", "x".repeat(41)]) expect((await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60, container })).status).toBe(400);
  // The owner's own session sees each container, and ends any one.
  expect((await rig.owner.get("all")).data.containers.map((c) => [c.owner, c.container, c.up])).toEqual([["owner", "default", true], ["via:owner", "job", true], ["worker:brain-x-reader", "default", true]]);
  await rig.owner.post("end", { owner: "worker:brain-x-reader", image: "node", container: "default" });
  expect(rig.fake.of("worker:brain-x-reader/default").running).toBe(false);
  // The limits count containers with time left. One that has time is extended at the limit.
  expect((await rig.owner.post("settings", { maxContainers: 2, maxPerOwner: 1 })).data).toEqual({ maxContainers: 2, maxPerOwner: 1 });
  expect((await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60, container: "second" })).data).toMatchObject({ error: "TooManyContainers" });
  expect((await reader.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60 })).data).toMatchObject({ error: "TooManyContainers" });
  expect((await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60 })).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await rig.owner.post("settings", { maxContainers: 0 })).status).toBe(400);
  // Not more containers than the max of the image, which is what Cloudflare runs.
  expect([(await rig.owner.post("settings", { maxContainers: 7 })).data.message, (await rig.owner.post("settings", { maxContainers: 6, maxPerOwner: 20 })).data]).toEqual(["maxContainers: a whole number from 1 to 6", { maxContainers: 6, maxPerOwner: 20 }]);
  return rig.sim.boxes.size + " containers of 3 owners";
}
// %%
test_container_that_cloudflare_does_not_give_answers_503_and_keeps_the_time = {
  const rig = await containerRig();
  rig.fake.of().refuse = "There is no container instance that can be provided to this Durable Object, try again later";
  const out = await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60 });
  expect([out.status, out.data.error]).toEqual([503, "ContainerNotReady"]);
  expect(out.data.message).toContain("There is no container instance");
  // The time is bought: the lease, the row and the alarm are there, and the next call starts the container.
  expect([out.data.paidUntil, rig.sim.rows.get("c/owner/node/default").paidUntil, rig.box().alarm]).toEqual([rig.lease().paidUntil, rig.lease().paidUntil, rig.lease().paidUntil]);
  expect((await rig.owner.get("status")).data).toMatchObject({ up: false, exit: "There is no container instance that can be provided to this Durable Object, try again later" });
  rig.fake.of().refuse = null;
  expect((await rig.owner.post("exec", { cmd: ["true"] })).status).toBe(200);
  // internet=false is read at the start.
  await rig.owner.post("extend", {}, { seconds: 60, container: "shut", internet: "false" });
  expect([rig.fake.of("owner/shut").starts, rig.lease("owner/shut").internet]).toEqual([[{ enableInternet: false }], false]);
  return "503, then up";
}
// %%
test_container_panel_shows_the_price_and_names_the_container = {
  const calls = [];
  const status = { owner: "owner", container: "default", image: "node", remaining: 42, up: true, exit: null, settings: { maxContainers: 6, maxPerOwner: 3 } };
  const fleet = { containers: [{ owner: "owner", image: "node", container: "default", up: true, remaining: 42 }, { owner: "worker:brain-x-reader", image: "node", container: "job", up: true, remaining: 9 }] };
  const client = { query: async (name, params) => (calls.push([name, params]), name === "container.all" ? fleet : { ...status, container: params.container }), procedure: async (name, input, opts) => (calls.push([name, input, opts]), { added: 60, costUsd: 0.00012, cold: true, exitCode: 0, ms: 5, stdout: "v22\n", stderr: "" }) };
  const el = containerPanel({ client, owner: true });
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 0));
  expect([...el.querySelectorAll("button")].map((b) => b.textContent)).toEqual(["Refresh", "Stop", "Add time", "Run", "End chosen container", "Save limits"]);
  expect(el.textContent).toContain("42 s are bought for default (node). The container is up.");
  expect(el.textContent).toContain("60 s costs $0.00012, charged to your day. It is not given back.");
  expect(el.textContent).toContain("worker:brain-x-reader");
  [...el.querySelectorAll("button")].find((b) => b.textContent === "Add time").click();
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 0));
  // The seconds and the two names go in the query string.
  expect(calls.find((c) => c[0] === "container.extend")).toEqual(["container.extend", {}, { params: { seconds: "60", container: "default", image: "node" } }]);
  expect(el.textContent).toContain("60 s added, $0.00012, started");
  expect(containerPanel({ client, owner: false }).textContent).toMatch(/Sign in to a Brain as the owner/);
  return "2 containers, 6 buttons";
}
